## 25. Evidence Interpretation

The presence of observability evidence means:

```text
Runtime activity can be inspected and correlated.
```

It does not automatically mean:

```text
External system certified
```

or:

```text
Production governance accepted
```

or:

```text
External service availability guaranteed
```

Those conclusions require separate evidence.

---

## 26. Final Observability Statement

NICAI provides bounded runtime observability through trace identifiers, timestamped runtime events, structured logs, execution evidence, and replay-compatible records.

The observability layer supports:

```text
TRACEABILITY
+
CORRELATION
+
EXECUTION REVIEW
+
FAILURE INVESTIGATION
+
REPLAY ANALYSIS
+
INTEGRATION AUDITABILITY
```

without claiming ownership of external monitoring, registry, governance, or production acceptance systems.

---

## 27. Certification Boundary

Final certification remains subject to the applicable review authority.

Where evidence is not available:

```text
PENDING
```

Where implementation exists but independent certification has not occurred:

```text
NOT YET CERTIFIED
```

These statuses are intentional and prevent undocumented assumptions from being presented as verified facts.
